update public.company_faq set answer = $qd$If a revealed supplier does not respond within 5 working days of your payment (we chase them after 3 working days, and we make the final call on day 5), everything you paid is refunded. That supplier then owes the exact amount refunded to you (the 3% reveal fee), the payment processor fee QuotesDone could not recover (from Supplier Agreement v14), an AED 500 administrative fee, and simple interest at 12% a year (or the maximum lawful rate) from the due date, and is blocked from new matches until it is settled.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '32' and md5(answer) = '608b31209dc7692cf3984e1d43087b8f'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: exact amount refunded to you (the 3% reveal fee), an AED 500 administrative fee
update public.company_faq set answer = $qd$Refunds are returned to the customer's original payment method via Stripe, and every refund is decided by a person here — none is automatic. The ladder runs from the customer's payment: if the revealed supplier has not responded by working day 3, our Customer Success Director chases them with the customer copied; still silent on working day 5, it comes to us for the final call; no response to that and everything the customer paid (the 3% reveal fee) is refunded, with banks taking 7-14 working days to show it. The non-responding supplier then owes the exact amount refunded, the payment processor fee QuotesDone could not recover (from Supplier Agreement v14), plus an AED 500 administrative fee and 12% per annum simple interest from the due date (the rate agreed in Supplier Agreement v14; 9% under v13 or earlier), except where such a charge is not permitted under UAE law, and is held from new matches until it is settled. Working days are Monday to Friday, UAE public holidays excluded. Other refund requests made within the 5-working-day refund window are reviewed and, if valid, refunded the same way.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '167' and md5(answer) = '6f4c54ee707b5a464ed0f595da6d1854'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements:  (the 3% reveal fee and the card processing fee) | (the UAE statutory maximum) | exact amount refunded, plus an AED 500 administrative fee
update public.company_faq set answer = $qd$There is no commission on won jobs — you keep 100% of the job value. The only charge tied to a job is the non-response charge if you ignore a customer who paid to reveal you: the exact amount refunded to the customer (the 3% reveal fee), the payment processor fee QuotesDone could not recover (from Supplier Agreement v14), an AED 500 administrative fee, and simple interest at 12% a year (or the maximum lawful rate) from the due date.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '49' and md5(answer) = 'ce7a5de2a8b304df57bb36f24db9513e'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: exact amount refunded to the customer (the 3% reveal fee), an AED 500 administrative fee
update public.company_faq set answer = $qd$QuotesDone charges suppliers no commission on won jobs — suppliers keep 100% of the job value. The only amounts collected from suppliers are the annual subscription (AED 1,000/year, never applicable to the first 1,000 suppliers who registered, applying from the 1,001st registration onward with no fixed start date) and a non-response charge (the exact amount refunded to the customer, which is the 3% reveal fee, the payment processor fee QuotesDone could not recover (from Supplier Agreement v14) plus an AED 500 administrative fee and 12% per annum interest from the due date) if a supplier ignores a customer who paid to reveal them, applied except where not permitted under UAE law. The customer separately pays a 3% reveal fee only when they choose to reveal a supplier's contact details.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '169' and md5(answer) = '48ed6132745383c8ea98f851a1da4c96'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: exact amount refunded to the customer, which is the 3% reveal fee plus an AED 500 administrative fee
update public.agent_knowledge set content = $qd$The three tickets that account for most volume: "where are my quotes" (check the inquiry is rfq_ready and routed, not that suppliers are slow), "who is this supplier" (identity is withheld until the reveal fee is paid — this is the product, not a limitation), and "the supplier I paid to reveal is not answering". The third has a defined remedy and it must be quoted exactly: a revealed supplier has 5 working days from the customer's payment to respond; we chase them on working day 3 with the customer copied; still silent on working day 5, the founder is notified for his final call; no response to that and everything the customer paid (the 3% reveal fee) is REFUNDED (every refund is the founder's decision, never automatic; banks take 7-14 working days to show it) and a non-response charge - the exact amount refunded, the payment processor fee QuotesDone could not recover (from Supplier Agreement v14) plus an AED 500 administrative fee and 12% per annum interest from the due date - is billed to the supplier. Do not invent goodwill credits, do not quote an AED 500 admin fee to customers (it is founder-set and not in the customer terms), and never state a commission — there is none.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '7981' and md5(content) = '3b98f3e21afc5378c623bdd1f7aab95a'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements:  (the 3% reveal fee and the card processing fee) | exact amount refunded plus an AED 500 administrative fee
update public.agent_knowledge set content = $qd$Money model (current, authoritative — mirrors pricing_config and the signed agreements): customers pay a 3% REVEAL FEE (no cap) to unlock the supplier they choose. Suppliers pay NO commission on won work and no registration fee for the first 1,000 registrants, who are permanently exempt; AED 1,000/year applies to everyone after them, with NO calendar start date (founder, 6 Sep 2026). Non-responsive supplier (the refund ladder, founder ruling 6 Sep 2026, final): a revealed supplier has 5 working days from the customer's PAYMENT to respond; the Customer Success Director chases on working day 3 with the customer copied; still silent on working day 5, the founder is notified for his final call; no response to that and everything the customer paid (the 3% reveal fee) is refunded (the founder approves every refund, none is automatic; banks take 7-14 working days to show it) AND a non-response recovery charge - the exact amount refunded (the 3% reveal fee) + AED 500 administrative fee + 12% per annum simple interest from the due date - is billed to the supplier as a due; the supplier is blocked from new matching until it is paid (repeat offenders removed). Off-platform circumvention (supplier or customer): AED 20,000 liquidated sum per incident or five (5) times the fee, whichever is higher, plus the unpaid fee + suspension, with a cure notice for an inadvertent first breach. Overdue supplier dues are recoverable in UAE courts; late-payment interest follows the signed Supplier Agreement — currently 12% per annum, SIMPLE interest, total interest capped at the principal (Federal Decree-Law 50/2022). The AED 500 admin fee per refund claim is founder-set but NOT yet written into the Supplier Agreement or Customer Terms, so it is not contractually recoverable until the terms are amended — do not include it in demand letters. There is NO commission and NO 2% fee of any kind — never quote those.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '3' and md5(content) = 'ac85244f825df3e60879e880786b2703'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements:  (the 3% reveal fee and the card processing fee)
update public.agent_knowledge set content = $qd$QUOTESDONE COMPANY FAQ — canonical answers every agent must use verbatim-in-spirit (founder-approved). If asked anything here, answer consistently with this. Do not contradict it or invent beyond it.

