update public.kb_chunks set content = $qd$## [Company Policies] Refund policy
Refunds are returned to the customer's original payment method via Stripe, and every refund is decided by a person here — none is automatic. The ladder runs from the customer's payment: if the revealed supplier has not responded by working day 3, our Customer Success Director chases them with the customer copied; still silent on working day 5, it comes to us for the final call; no response to that and everything the customer paid (the 3% reveal fee) is refunded, with banks taking 7-14 working days to show it. The non-responding supplier then owes the exact amount refunded, the payment processor fee QuotesDone could not recover (from Supplier Agreement v14), plus an AED 500 administrative fee and 12% per annum simple interest from the due date (the rate agreed in Supplier Agreement v14; 9% under v13 or earlier), except where such a charge is not permitted under UAE law, and is held from new matches until it is settled. Working days are Monday to Friday, UAE public holidays excluded. Other refund requests made within the 5-working-day refund window are reviewed and, if valid, refunded the same way.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '174367' and md5(content) = '8ce2b16e2400e72ffa9a215520c8c4b6'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements:  (the 3% reveal fee and the card processing fee) | (the UAE statutory maximum) | exact amount refunded, plus an AED 500 administrative fee
update public.kb_chunks set content = $qd$You are a credit-control / accounts-receivable specialist with 10+ years in UAE B2B collections. Suppliers owe NO commission on won work. The only supplier dues you chase are: (a) the non-response recovery charge — the reveal fee refunded to the customer when a revealed supplier stayed silent through the 5-working-day ladder from the customer's payment (the Customer Success Director chases on working day 3, the founder makes his final call on day 5), plus the AED 500 administrative fee and 12% per annum simple interest — and (b) the off-platform circumvention sum (AED 20,000 per incident or five times the fee, whichever is higher, plus the unpaid fee) where invoked. Cadence: portal reminder on billing; on overdue, email from supplier@quotesdone.com citing the accepted Supplier Agreement and applying late-payment interest per that agreement (currently 12% per annum, simple, capped at the principal); the supplier stays blocked from new matching until the due is paid; at 30 working days escalate and alert the founder. The AED 500 admin fee is NOT yet in the signed terms — do not demand it until the agreement is amended. Tone: firm, factual, professional; always reference the accepted Terms. Hand the worst cases to the Legal agent for a demand letter. Never threaten amounts beyond the Terms.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '178531' and md5(content) = 'e0957bb79109b1e1ded87122966919d6';
update public.kb_chunks set content = $qd$Operate to Chartered Institute of Credit Management (CICM) standards. Track DSO, aging buckets (current / 1-14wd / 15-30wd / 30+wd), and collection effectiveness. Run a structured dunning cadence: billing notice -> overdue notice citing the contractual basis -> final notice -> hand to Legal. Match tone to payer history (gentle for good payers, firm for repeat late). Always quote the accepted Supplier Agreement and the exact amount. Know when to stop chasing and escalate to a Payment Order. The only recoverable items are: the non-response recovery charge (equal to the exact amount refunded to the customer (the reveal fee)), the AED 20,000 circumvention sum, late-payment interest per the signed agreement (12% per annum simple, capped at principal), and matching-block until payment. Never invent or threaten charges beyond the signed Terms; the AED 500 admin fee stays out of demands until the terms are amended to include it.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '178532' and md5(content) = '169f22c8681ac3548207f0f79ea09064';
update public.kb_chunks set content = $qd$Escalation ladder for unpaid supplier dues (non-response recovery charge equal to the exact amount refunded to the customer (the reveal fee), or the AED 20,000 circumvention sum — there is no commission on won work): (1) system reminders; (2) Letter of Demand giving 7 days; (3) formal Legal Notice (may be served via Notary Public); (4) Payment Order petition or Statement of Claim before the Dubai Courts for the due + contractual late-payment interest per the signed Supplier Agreement — currently 12% per annum, simple, total interest capped at the principal (Law 50/2022) — + legal costs. Do NOT claim the AED 500 admin fee in any demand or pleading until it is written into the Supplier Agreement (it is founder-set but not yet contractually recoverable; recommend the amendment). Rely on the electronically accepted Supplier Agreement (Decree-Law 46/2021) as the contract, and the platform records as evidence. Always work from the exact figures the Collections agent provides.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '178526' and md5(content) = '3dcf66109e0619a4fcb26ae955605d65';
update public.kb_chunks set content = $qd$Fees (LIVE): buyer REVEAL FEE = 3% of quote value, currently effectively UNCAPPED (lower cap / first-reveal-free discussed, not live). NO commission on won work. Supplier registration FREE for EVERY supplier until 31 July 2027; AED 1,000/year begins 1 August 2027; the first 1,000 registered suppliers are exempt PERMANENTLY. Dormant today - all free-tier. Money via Stripe both ways; QuotesDone never holds supplier bank details. REFUNDS (unresponsive supplier): 3-working-day window (after 1wd Notify supplier, after 3wd Request refund -> founder approval), payout 7-14 wd after approval, 3% processing deduction. Recover from an unreachable supplier: reveal fee + 12%/annum simple late fee per the signed Supplier Agreement (Fed Decree-Law 50/2022 caps total interest at principal). The AED 500 admin fee per claim is founder-set but NOT yet written into the signed terms — exclude it from demands and pleadings until the agreement is amended.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '178189' and md5(content) = '2d92d777c21863dda55ec816b352deea';
update public.kb_chunks set content = $qd$## [Company Policies] Commission policy
QuotesDone charges suppliers no commission on won jobs — suppliers keep 100% of the job value. The only amounts collected from suppliers are the annual subscription (AED 1,000/year, never applicable to the first 1,000 suppliers who registered, applying from the 1,001st registration onward with no fixed start date) and a non-response charge (the exact amount refunded to the customer, which is the 3% reveal fee, the payment processor fee QuotesDone could not recover (from Supplier Agreement v14) plus an AED 500 administrative fee and 12% per annum interest from the due date) if a supplier ignores a customer who paid to reveal them, applied except where not permitted under UAE law. The customer separately pays a 3% reveal fee only when they choose to reveal a supplier's contact details.$qd$, embedding_gte = null where id = '174369' and md5(content) = '63fff0bbb7624c5bec9fd6412d20694e'; -- ALSO worded against canonical_statements: exact amount refunded to the customer, which is the 3% reveal fee plus an AED 500 administrative fee

-- policy keys
insert into public.decision_policy (key, value, description) values ('refund_admin_fee_aed', to_jsonb(500::numeric), $qd$what the seats and the customer texts state (fn_company_hard_rules, fn_company_self_knowledge_sync, fn_refund_amount_aed). Source: src/content/company_facts.json 2026-09-24.2.$qd$)
  on conflict (key) do update set value = excluded.value, updated_at = now();
insert into public.decision_policy (key, value, description) values ('supplier_nonresponse_admin_fee_from_v13_aed', to_jsonb(500::numeric), $qd$what fn_accountant_nonresponse_charge charges a supplier who accepted v13 or later before the reveal. Source: src/content/company_facts.json 2026-09-24.2.$qd$)
  on conflict (key) do update set value = excluded.value, updated_at = now();
